{% comment %}
  ZINSETT "Homestead Supply" design tokens.

  Source of truth: ops/design/redesign/FINAL-SPEC.md §1 (token table) — the
  approved re-skin of the retired "Warm Field" direction. This is a VALUE
  swap on the existing --zinsett-* names wherever a role correspondence
  exists (see FINAL-SPEC §1.1), plus the small set of new custom properties
  Warm Field had no slot for (§1.2 wells, kraft, cream-ink, shadow/focus
  colors) and a dual light/dark theme layer Warm Field never had.

  Concept: the modern general store / feed-supply ledger — color-blocked
  bands of cream, kraft, and barn green; wood-type slab headlines; prices
  as physical shelf tags; trust marks as rubber stamps; red rationed to
  sale + stamps (~2% of the page). Hard corners everywhere (radius 0);
  hard offset shadows (no blur).

  Theme plumbing (FINAL-SPEC §1.2 "Theme plumbing"): tokens declared on
  :root (light/"day ledger" default), redefined under
  `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` ("lantern ledger") AND under
  explicit `:root[data-theme="dark"]` / `:root[data-theme="light"]`
  attribute overrides so a future site-wide toggle beats the OS preference
  in both directions. `color-scheme: light dark` is declared on :root and
  re-pinned per theme (judge flag: color-scheme hygiene, applied
  preemptively) — paired with `<meta name="color-scheme" content="light
  dark">` in layout/theme.liquid.

  Pinned (theme-independent) inks (FINAL-SPEC §1.2 "Pinned inks"): the
  photo "well" mounting-card stays light in BOTH themes (so
  mix-blend-mode: multiply keeps working on dark backgrounds), so text set
  on a well (price-tag numerals, hero-card title) and the rationed stamp
  device use --zinsett-color-well-ink / --zinsett-color-stamp — declared
  once on :root and never overridden in the dark/media blocks below.

  - Typography family/style stay settings-driven (font_picker:
    type_header_font for the slab display face, type_body_font for the
    sans body face) so Theme Settings > Typography remains the single
    control surface; the FINAL-SPEC §1.5 fallback stacks are literal
    (not settings-driven) and appended after the picked font, same
    mechanism as before.
  - The ledger mono voice (eyebrows, stamps, announcement, meta rows) is
    now self-hosted per FINAL-SPEC §1.5: IBM Plex Mono Regular (400) +
    SemiBold (600), Latin-subset WOFF2s (SIL OFL 1.1, IBM Corp.,
    github.com/IBM/plex), vendored at `assets/zinsett-plex-mono-400.woff2`
    / `-600.woff2` (~35KB combined). @font-face declared once below (this
    snippet is rendered a single time from layout/theme.liquid) with
    `font-display: swap`; the judge-fixed `ui-monospace` system chain
    stays as the fallback tail on --zinsett-font-mono-family so text never
    goes invisible while the webfont loads.
  - Colors, type scale, spacing, radius, shadow, and motion are literal
    per FINAL-SPEC — this file is the one place those hex/values live.

  Rendered from layout/theme.liquid before Dawn's own settings-driven
  `:root` / `.color-*` style block so Dawn's cascade still wins for its own
  --color-*/--font-*-family variables while --zinsett-* stays available
  everywhere as the brand-token layer.
{% endcomment %}
{%- style -%}
  /* IBM Plex Mono (SIL OFL 1.1) — self-hosted per FINAL-SPEC §1.5. Only
     the two weights the ledger voice actually uses (body-weight-bold
     equivalents: 400 meta/labels, 600 stamps/prices) to keep the added
     weight small; the 400 file is also preloaded in layout/theme.liquid
     since it's used above the fold on card price chips. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono';
    src: url('{{ 'zinsett-plex-mono-400.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono';
    src: url('{{ 'zinsett-plex-mono-600.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    color-scheme: light dark;

    /* color/* — FINAL-SPEC §1.1 "day ledger" (light, default) */
    --zinsett-color-paper: #F8EED6;
    --zinsett-color-paper-2: #F2E2BE;
    --zinsett-color-kraft: #DCB273;
    --zinsett-color-kraft-deep: #B9863C;
    --zinsett-color-ink: #201909;
    --zinsett-color-ink-soft: #4C4028;
    --zinsett-color-card: #F8EED6;
    --zinsett-color-terra: #1E4230; /* CTA role passes to barn green (§1.1) */
    --zinsett-color-terra-deep: #142B1F;
    --zinsett-color-green: #1E4230;
    --zinsett-color-red: #A9391F;
    --zinsett-color-cream-ink: #F6ECD2;
    --zinsett-color-cream-soft: #CBBF9F;
    --zinsett-color-well: #F3E6C4;
    --zinsett-color-well-line: #D9C08B;
    --zinsett-color-well-cool: #E9EACF;
    --zinsett-color-well-cool-line: #C6C793;
    --zinsett-color-shadow: #201909;
    --zinsett-color-focus: #A9391F;

    /* --zinsett-color-gold is RETIRED (§1.1) — nearest successor for
       decorative rules/marks/numerals is --zinsett-color-kraft-deep
       (never text: 2.6:1 on paper). Do not reintroduce --zinsett-color-gold. */

    /* 1px hairlines / secondary text stay dynamic against ink so they flip
       for free with the theme blocks below — no per-theme redeclaration. */
    --zinsett-color-line: color-mix(in srgb, var(--zinsett-color-ink) 22%, transparent);
    --zinsett-color-muted: var(--zinsett-color-ink-soft);

    /* Pinned inks (§1.2) — wells stay light in both themes, so text set on
       a well and the rationed stamp device do NOT flip with the theme. */
    --zinsett-color-well-ink: #201909;
    --zinsett-color-stamp: #A9391F;

    /* type/display — slab display face (Roboto Slab 800 via the Shopify
       font library; upgrade path Clarendon Graphic/Sentinel Black if
       licensed). Fallback stack is FINAL-SPEC §1.5's mockup system stack. */
    --zinsett-font-display-family:
      {{ settings.type_header_font.family }}, 'Rockwell Nova', 'Rockwell', 'Roboto Slab', 'Bookman Old Style', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    --zinsett-font-display-style: {{ settings.type_header_font.style }};
    --zinsett-font-display-weight-semibold: 700;
    --zinsett-font-display-weight-bold: 800;

    /* type/body — sans body face (Archivo via the Shopify font library;
       fallback Source Sans 3). Fallback stack per FINAL-SPEC §1.5. */
    --zinsett-font-body-family:
      {{ settings.type_body_font.family }}, 'Avenir Next', 'Avenir', 'Seravek', 'Trebuchet MS', Verdana, system-ui, sans-serif;
    --zinsett-font-body-style: {{ settings.type_body_font.style }};
    --zinsett-font-body-weight-regular: 400;
    --zinsett-font-body-weight-medium: 500;
    --zinsett-font-body-weight-semibold: 600;

    /* type/mono — the ledger voice (eyebrows, stamps, announcement, meta
       rows). IBM Plex Mono is now self-hosted (@font-face above) per
       FINAL-SPEC §1.5; the judge-fixed `ui-monospace` system stack from
       the mockup stays as the fallback tail. Weight 600 (SemiBold) is the
       heaviest we ship, so --font-mono-weight-bold maps to it rather than
       the old 700 (no 700 binary is vendored — avoids a synthetic-bold
       fallback flash). */
    --zinsett-font-mono-family:
      'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, 'Cascadia Mono', 'Segoe UI Mono', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', monospace;
    --zinsett-font-mono-weight-bold: 600;

    /*
      type/scale — FINAL-SPEC §1.3 replaces the old px-labelled scale's
      VALUES while keeping the 8 slot names (Dawn's root font-size is
      `62.5%`, i.e. 1rem = 10px here, vs. the mockup's unscaled 16px root —
      every mockup rem value below is carried in at ×1.6 so on-screen sizes
      match the approved mockup exactly). Roles, smallest to largest:
        scale-12   -> meta        (.6rem  mockup -> .96rem)  card meta row, flags, stamps
        scale-13-5 -> eyebrow/mono(.72rem mockup -> 1.152rem) kickers, announcement, ledger labels
        scale-15   -> note        (.85rem mockup -> 1.36rem) card concrete-fact line ("base" alias)
        scale-18   -> card-title  (1.02rem mockup -> 1.632rem) product names, tile labels
        scale-22   -> stat/price  (interpolated — no direct §1.3 row; large
                                    numerals e.g. BundleBlock price display)
        scale-27   -> h2          (clamp(1.9rem,3.6vw,3rem) mockup -> clamp(3.04rem,3.6vw,4.8rem))
        scale-34   -> h2-editorial(clamp(2.1rem,4.4vw,3.6rem) mockup -> clamp(3.36rem,4.4vw,5.76rem))
        scale-44   -> display     (clamp(2.5rem,6.2vw,4.9rem) mockup -> clamp(4rem,6.2vw,7.84rem))
      Every numeral in prices/counts/stats gets `font-variant-numeric:
      tabular-nums` at the call site (keyword, not a token — not a color).
    */
    --zinsett-type-scale-12: 0.96rem;
    --zinsett-type-scale-13-5: 1.152rem;
    --zinsett-type-scale-15: 1.36rem;
    --zinsett-type-scale-18: 1.632rem;
    --zinsett-type-scale-22: 2rem;
    --zinsett-type-scale-27: clamp(3.04rem, 3.6vw, 4.8rem);
    --zinsett-type-scale-34: clamp(3.36rem, 4.4vw, 5.76rem);
    --zinsett-type-scale-44: clamp(4rem, 6.2vw, 7.84rem);
    --zinsett-type-scale-base: var(--zinsett-type-scale-15);

    /* Legacy named aliases (kept for back-compat; values now follow the
       Homestead role each slot holds per the ladder above). */
    --zinsett-type-display-44: var(--zinsett-type-scale-44);
    --zinsett-type-display-34: var(--zinsett-type-scale-34);
    --zinsett-type-h2-27: var(--zinsett-type-scale-27);
    --zinsett-type-h3-22: var(--zinsett-type-scale-22);
    --zinsett-type-body-15: var(--zinsett-type-scale-15);
    --zinsett-type-small-13-5: var(--zinsett-type-scale-13-5);
    --zinsett-type-caption-12: var(--zinsett-type-scale-12);

    /* New FINAL-SPEC-named aliases (§1.3 role names) for new Homestead
       component CSS to reach for directly instead of the numbered slots. */
    --zinsett-type-display: var(--zinsett-type-scale-44);
    --zinsett-type-h2-editorial: var(--zinsett-type-scale-34);
    --zinsett-type-h2: var(--zinsett-type-scale-27);
    --zinsett-type-card-title: var(--zinsett-type-scale-18);
    --zinsett-type-note: var(--zinsett-type-scale-15);
    --zinsett-type-eyebrow: var(--zinsett-type-scale-13-5);
    --zinsett-type-meta: var(--zinsett-type-scale-12);
    --zinsett-type-body: 1.6rem;

    /* space — unchanged 4/8/16/24/40/64 scale (Warm Field). FINAL-SPEC's
       fluid section-block/grid-gap clamps are additive, new tokens below;
       the existing discrete scale keeps serving every current call site. */
    --zinsett-space-4: 0.4rem;
    --zinsett-space-8: 0.8rem;
    --zinsett-space-16: 1.6rem;
    --zinsett-space-24: 2.4rem;
    --zinsett-space-40: 4rem;
    --zinsett-space-64: 6.4rem;

    /* New fluid spacing (FINAL-SPEC §1.4) for Homestead section/grid work. */
    --zinsett-space-section: clamp(4.16rem, 6vw, 7.68rem);
    --zinsett-space-grid-gap: clamp(1.28rem, 1.6vw, 2.08rem);

    /* radius — FINAL-SPEC §1.4: hard corners are the direction. 0 on
       cards/inputs; pill kept (999px) but UNUSED for badges/chips/bars —
       circles only on the price-tag punch-hole and focus-ring rounding. */
    --zinsett-radius-card: 0;
    --zinsett-radius-input: 0;
    --zinsett-radius-pill: 999px;

    /* shadow — hard offset only, no blur (FINAL-SPEC §1.4). Scale: 3px
       add/cart buttons, 4px cards/aisles/buttons (default), 8px hero/bird
       showpieces. --zinsett-shadow kept as the legacy alias name. */
    --zinsett-shadow-sm: 3px 3px 0 var(--zinsett-color-shadow);
    --zinsett-shadow-default: 4px 4px 0 var(--zinsett-color-shadow);
    --zinsett-shadow-lg: 8px 8px 0 var(--zinsett-color-shadow);
    --zinsett-shadow: var(--zinsett-shadow-default);

    /* border scale (FINAL-SPEC §1.4), for new Homestead component CSS. */
    --zinsett-border-structural: 3px solid var(--zinsett-color-ink);
    --zinsett-border-component: 2px solid var(--zinsett-color-ink);
    --zinsett-border-hairline: 1px solid var(--zinsett-color-line);
    --zinsett-border-trust: 2px dashed var(--zinsett-color-kraft-deep);

    /* motion — 120ms ease hovers (translate/box-shadow only, FINAL-SPEC
       §1.4); reveal timing unchanged (reduce-motion block below kills both). */
    --zinsett-motion-hover-duration: 120ms;
    --zinsett-motion-hover-easing: ease;
    --zinsett-motion-reveal-duration: 320ms;
    --zinsett-motion-reveal-easing: ease;

    /* grid — container converts FINAL-SPEC's 76rem (16px root) max-width
       to the 1216px it renders as; unaffected by Dawn's rem rescale since
       it's expressed in px. Column/gutter scale otherwise unchanged. */
    --zinsett-grid-columns: 12;
    --zinsett-grid-columns-mobile: 4;
    --zinsett-grid-max-width: 1216px;
    --zinsett-grid-gutter: 2.4rem;
    --zinsett-grid-gutter-mobile: 1.6rem;
  }

  /* "lantern ledger" — dark, OS-preference-driven (FINAL-SPEC §1.1/§1.2). */
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --zinsett-color-paper: #191510;
      --zinsett-color-paper-2: #221C13;
      --zinsett-color-kraft: #4A3A1D;
      --zinsett-color-kraft-deep: #6E5527;
      --zinsett-color-ink: #F1E5C6;
      --zinsett-color-ink-soft: #C8B888;
      --zinsett-color-card: #191510;
      --zinsett-color-terra: #1B3A28;
      --zinsett-color-terra-deep: #122619;
      --zinsett-color-green: #1B3A28;
      --zinsett-color-red: #E58562;
      --zinsett-color-cream-ink: #F1E5C6;
      --zinsett-color-cream-soft: #BFB292;
      --zinsett-color-well: #EADCB6;
      --zinsett-color-well-line: #C9AE77;
      --zinsett-color-well-cool: #DEE0BE;
      --zinsett-color-well-cool-line: #A9AB77;
      --zinsett-color-shadow: #000000;
      --zinsett-color-focus: #E5A05E;
      /* --zinsett-color-well-ink / --zinsett-color-stamp intentionally NOT
         redeclared here — pinned per §1.2, the well stays light so text on
         it (and the stamp) keep their day-ledger ink in both themes. */
    }
  }

  /* Toggle-proof overrides (FINAL-SPEC §1.2 "theme plumbing") — win over
     the OS preference in both directions once a site toggle sets
     `data-theme` on the root element. No toggle ships in this pass; these
     are pre-wired so one can be added without touching this token layer. */
  :root[data-theme='light'] {
    color-scheme: light;
    --zinsett-color-paper: #F8EED6;
    --zinsett-color-paper-2: #F2E2BE;
    --zinsett-color-kraft: #DCB273;
    --zinsett-color-kraft-deep: #B9863C;
    --zinsett-color-ink: #201909;
    --zinsett-color-ink-soft: #4C4028;
    --zinsett-color-card: #F8EED6;
    --zinsett-color-terra: #1E4230;
    --zinsett-color-terra-deep: #142B1F;
    --zinsett-color-green: #1E4230;
    --zinsett-color-red: #A9391F;
    --zinsett-color-cream-ink: #F6ECD2;
    --zinsett-color-cream-soft: #CBBF9F;
    --zinsett-color-well: #F3E6C4;
    --zinsett-color-well-line: #D9C08B;
    --zinsett-color-well-cool: #E9EACF;
    --zinsett-color-well-cool-line: #C6C793;
    --zinsett-color-shadow: #201909;
    --zinsett-color-focus: #A9391F;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --zinsett-color-paper: #191510;
    --zinsett-color-paper-2: #221C13;
    --zinsett-color-kraft: #4A3A1D;
    --zinsett-color-kraft-deep: #6E5527;
    --zinsett-color-ink: #F1E5C6;
    --zinsett-color-ink-soft: #C8B888;
    --zinsett-color-card: #191510;
    --zinsett-color-terra: #1B3A28;
    --zinsett-color-terra-deep: #122619;
    --zinsett-color-green: #1B3A28;
    --zinsett-color-red: #E58562;
    --zinsett-color-cream-ink: #F1E5C6;
    --zinsett-color-cream-soft: #BFB292;
    --zinsett-color-well: #EADCB6;
    --zinsett-color-well-line: #C9AE77;
    --zinsett-color-well-cool: #DEE0BE;
    --zinsett-color-well-cool-line: #A9AB77;
    --zinsett-color-shadow: #000000;
    --zinsett-color-focus: #E5A05E;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    :root {
      --zinsett-motion-hover-duration: 0ms;
      --zinsett-motion-reveal-duration: 0ms;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
